r boutiques, upscale cafes, K-beauty clinics and some of the city's best restaurants hide behind glass facades.","nearestMetro":"Gangnam (Line 2)","vibe":"Upscale & polished","bestFor":["Cafes","Shopping","Fine dining","K-beauty"],"priceRange":"₩₩₩ – ₩₩₩₩"}}]}],["$","div","myeongdong",{"className":"flex-shrink-0 w-64 sm:w-auto","children":["$","$L12",null,{"neighbourhood":{"slug":"myeongdong","name":"Myeongdong","citySlug":"seoul","image":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1498654896293-37aacf113fd9?w=1200&q=80","intro":"Seoul's ultimate shopping district and street food paradise. Myeongdong's neon-lit streets are packed with K-beauty stores, department stores and some of the best street food vendors in the city. Touristy but worth it.","nearestMetro":"Myeongdong (Line 4)","vibe":"Buzzing & commercial","bestFor":["Street food","Shopping","K-beauty","Tourism"],"priceRange":"₩ – ₩₩₩"}}]}],["$","div","insadong",{"className":"flex-shrink-0 w-64 sm:w-auto","children":["$","$L12",null,{"neighbourhood":{"slug":"insadong","name":"Insadong","citySlug":"seoul","image":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1517154421773-0529f29ea451?w=1200&q=80","intro":"Seoul's cultural heart. Traditional teahouses, antique shops, art galleries and hanok alleyways make Insadong the place to experience old Korea in the middle of a modern city. Don't miss the Ssamziegil complex.","nearestMetro":"Anguk (Line 3)","vibe":"Traditional & artsy","bestFor":["Culture","Tea","Art galleries","Souvenirs"],"priceRange":"₩₩"}}]}],["$","div","apgujeong",{"className":"flex-shrink-0 w-64 sm:w-auto","children":["$","$L12",null,{"neighbourhood":{"slug":"apgujeong","name":"Apgujeong","citySlug":"seoul","image":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1559305616-3f99cd43e353?w=1200&q=80","intro":"Seoul's most fashionable neighbourhood. Apgujeong Rodeo is where K-pop stars shop, where new restaurants open first and where Seoul's trend-conscious crowd comes to see and be seen.","nearestMetro":"Apgujeong Rodeo (Bundang Line)","vibe":"Trendy & luxurious","bestFor":["Fashion","Fine dining","People watching","K-pop culture"],"priceRange":"₩₩₩ – ₩₩₩₩"}}]}],["$","div","jamsil",{"className":"flex-shrink-0 w-64 sm:w-auto","children":["$","$L12",null,{"neighbourhood":{"slug":"jamsil","name":"Jamsil","citySlug":"seoul","image":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1617469767053-d3b523a0b982?w=1200&q=80","intro":"Home to Lotte World, the Olympic Park and Seoul's modern entertainment district. Jamsil combines family-friendly attractions with excellent shopping at Lotte World Mall and surprisingly good local food spots.","nearestMetro":"Jamsil (Line 2/8)","vibe":"Entertainment & family","bestFor":["Theme parks","Shopping","Sports","Lake walks"],"priceRange":"₩₩ – ₩₩₩"}}]}],["$","div","garosu-gil",{"className":"flex-shrink-0 w-64 sm:w-auto","children":["$","$L12",null,{"neighbourhood":{"slug":"garosu-gil","name":"Garosu-gil","citySlug":"seoul","image":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1559305616-3f99cd43e353?w=1200&q=80","intro":"Tree-lined street in Sinsa-dong famous for indie boutiques, design shops and cafes. A quieter, more refined alternative to Gangnam Station with a strong fashion and brunch scene.","nearestMetro":"Sinsa (Line 3)","vibe":"Trendy & leafy","bestFor":["Cafes","Fashion","Brunch","Design"],"priceRange":"₩₩₩"}}]}],["$","div","seongsu",{"className":"flex-shrink-0 w-64 sm:w-auto","children":["$","$L12",null,{"neighbourhood":{"slug":"seongsu","name":"Seongsu","citySlug":"seoul","image":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1544735716-392fe2489ffa?w=1200&q=80","intro":"The 'Brooklyn of Seoul'. Former shoe factories turned into cafes, galleries and concept stores. Seongsu has become the go-to area for creative types and specialty coffee.","nearestMetro":"Seongsu (Line 2)","vibe":"Industrial & creative","bestFor":["Cafes","Art","Shopping","Photo spots"],"priceRange":"₩₩ – ₩₩₩"}}]}],["$","div","yeonnam",{"className":"flex-shrink-0 w-64 sm:w-auto","children":["$","$L12",null,{"neighbourhood":{"